= Medical Termination of Pregnancy

No couple plans for a pregnancy to end. Yet some pregnancies cannot continue
safely — the mother's health is in danger, the foetus has a serious defect, or
the pregnancy followed a crime such as rape. When a pregnancy is ended
*deliberately*, by choice and by medical procedure, it is called *MTP (medical
termination of pregnancy)* — an intentional or voluntary abortion. India made
this safe and legal nearly fifty years ago, and the rules form an exam-table
students must memorise precisely.

- *The definition:* MTP is the intentional or voluntary termination of
  pregnancy before full term, performed as a medical procedure.
- *The law:* MTP is legal in India under the *Medical Termination of Pregnancy
  Act, 1971*, amended in 2017 and again in 2021 to widen safe access.
- *Not the same as miscarriage:* a miscarriage is a *spontaneous* abortion —
  the body ends the pregnancy on its own; MTP is a *chosen* medical act.

== The legal windows, week by week

#table(
  columns: (1.1fr, 1.5fr, 1.2fr),
  table.header[*Stage of pregnancy*][*What the law allows*][*Who certifies it*],
  [Up to 12 weeks (first trimester)],
  [MTP may be performed — this is the safest and most common window.],
  [One registered medical practitioner.],
  [12 to 24 weeks (second trimester)],
  [MTP may still be performed, with extra care and two medical opinions.],
  [Opinion of registered medical practitioners.],
  [Beyond 24 weeks],
  [Only in narrow special cases — for example, severe foetal abnormality or a serious risk to the mother's life (2021 amendment).],
  [A medical board of specialists.],
)

- *Why the first 12 weeks matter:* the earlier the termination, the simpler
  the procedure; the risk rises steadily after the first trimester.
- *The methods in one line:* early pregnancies are ended by *suction or
  vacuum aspiration* (gentle suction empties the uterus) or by *medicines*;
  later ones may need surgery.
- *Qualified hands only:* MTP must be done by a qualified, registered doctor
  in an approved facility — never by unqualified practitioners.

== The cost of unsafe abortion

- *The danger list:* unsafe abortions — done by untrained hands in unhygienic
  conditions — cause heavy bleeding, severe infection and even death.
- *The lasting damage:* an unsafe procedure can scar the reproductive tract
  and leave a woman *infertile* for life.
- *The social point:* legal, safe MTP exists precisely so that no woman has
  to risk her life in secret; restricting access does not stop MTPs, it only
  makes them dangerous.
- *The partner's role:* a safe MTP also needs a supportive family — secrecy
  and stigma are what push women toward unsafe hands.
- *The numbers to memorise:* 12 and 24 — the two week-marks that carry every
  MTP question, tied to the words "first trimester" and "second trimester".
- *Who may certify:* a *registered medical practitioner* — a doctor with a
  recognised qualification, entered on a state medical register, working at
  an approved facility.
- *The counselling rule:* good doctors pair MTP with counselling and
  contraception advice, so the next pregnancy is a planned one.

== Worked Example — Applying the legal windows

- *Case A — a woman is 8 weeks pregnant and requests termination:* this is
  the first trimester. One registered medical practitioner can certify it,
  and the procedure is at its safest — suction aspiration or medicines.
- *Case B — a foetal abnormality is suspected at 15 weeks:* the second
  trimester window (12–24 weeks) still allows MTP, with the opinion of
  registered medical practitioners, and carries more procedural risk.
- *Case C — a request arrives at 27 weeks:* beyond 24 weeks, only narrow
  special cases qualify — a medical board weighs severe foetal abnormality
  or danger to the mother's life (the 2021 amendment). An ordinary request
  does not qualify.
- *Case D — a pregnancy that followed rape, at 11 weeks:* the first-trimester
  window applies with one practitioner's opinion; the law names such cases
  specifically and keeps the procedure confidential.

