  [Chlamydiasis], [*Chlamydia* (bacterium)], [Bacterial], [Often symptomless — a classic silent spreader.],
  [Genital herpes], [*Herpes simplex virus*], [Viral], [Painful blisters that return; treatable, not curable.],
  [Genital warts], [*Human papilloma virus (HPV)*], [Viral], [Warts on the genitals; linked to cancers of the tract.],
  [Trichomoniasis], [*Trichomonas* (protozoan)], [Protozoan], [Causes frothy discharge; treatable with medicines.],
  [Hepatitis-B], [Hepatitis-B virus], [Viral], [Also spreads by shared needles and infected blood; damages the liver.],
  [HIV], [Human Immunodeficiency Virus], [Viral], [Attacks the immune system and leads to AIDS; also blood-borne.],
)

- *The curable half:* bacterial STIs — gonorrhoea, syphilis, chlamydiasis —
  are *completely curable* with antibiotics when caught early.
- *The stubborn half:* viral STIs — herpes, warts, hepatitis-B, HIV — can be
  *treated and controlled but never fully cured*; the virus stays in the body.
- *The extra routes:* hepatitis-B and HIV also spread through transfusion of
  infected blood and sharing of contaminated needles, not only through sex.

== Prevention: the working checklist

- *Condoms:* the single habit that blocks both pregnancy and STIs.
- *Fewer, safer choices:* avoiding sex with multiple partners cuts risk
  sharply; one infected partner can infect every partner that follows.
- *Hygiene and honesty:* personal cleanliness and open discussion before
  marriage protect couples — silence protects nobody.
- *Screened blood:* accept blood only from licensed, tested blood banks;
  insist on new, sterile needles.

== Worked Example — Reading a symptom report

A 24-year-old reports burning urination and a yellow discharge, three weeks
after a new partner. Walk the diagnosis the way a doctor would.

- *Step 1 — read the signs:* burning urination plus genital discharge point
  to a bacterial STI — gonorrhoea or chlamydiasis are the first suspects.
- *Step 2 — confirm the agent:* a swab test identifies *Neisseria
  gonorrhoeae* or *Chlamydia* under the microscope and in the lab.
- *Step 3 — treat early:* antibiotics *cure* bacterial STIs completely when
  started in time.
- *Step 4 — treat the pair:* the partner is tested and treated too, or the
  infection simply travels back and forth between the two.
- *Step 5 — the caution:* had the agent been a virus — herpes or HIV — the
  same report would end in treatment and control, never in cure.

