== Three checking habits that beat every trap above

- *Name the family, not just the device:* every contraceptive question is a
  family question — say "copper-releasing IUD" in your head, never just "Cu-T".
- *Route before method:* for ART, decide the destination first — uterus or
  tube — then check the blastomere count and the cargo (embryo or gametes).
- *Cure or control:* for STIs, make the bacterial-versus-viral split first;
  everything else — agent, treatment, prevention — follows from it.
- *Window before answer:* MTP and emergency pills are both questions of weeks
  and hours — memorise the numbers (12, 12–24, 72) and attach them to the
  right method.
- *Whose body?* vasectomy and tubectomy are mirror procedures for two
  partners; before answering, say the partner's name in your head.

