= Solutions

#solution(1, [Days 10 to 17 cover ovulation (near day 14) plus the survival margins of sperm (3–5 days) and the egg (1 day). Avoiding this fertile window is *periodic abstinence*. Withdrawal and coitus interruptus are two names for the same method, and lactational amenorrhoea depends on breastfeeding.], answer: "C")

#solution(2, [The copper in each name marks the *copper-releasing* family: copper ions suppress sperm motility and fertilising capacity. Lippes loop is the non-medicated device, while Progestasert and LNG-20 are the hormone-releasing IUDs.], answer: "B")

#solution(3, [Saheli contains *centchroman*, a *non-steroidal* pill taken *once a week* with hardly any side effects — developed in India. It is not an emergency pill (72-hour rule) and no pill blocks STIs.], answer: "C")

#solution(4, [In IVF the embryo grows outside and is transferred into the uterus at *8 or more blastomeres*. Earlier stages belong to ZIFT (up to 8 blastomeres), and gametes are never the IVF transfer.], answer: "D")

#solution(5, [ZIFT stands for Zygote Intrafallopian Transfer — the zygote or an early embryo of *up to 8 blastomeres* is placed into the *fallopian tube*, from where it travels down to the uterus naturally.], answer: "B")

#solution(6, [GIFT — Gamete Intrafallopian Transfer — moves *unfertilised gametes* (egg + sperm) into the tube, so fertilisation happens *inside the body*. ZIFT transfers a zygote, ICSI injects a sperm into an egg, and IUI places semen in the uterus.], answer: "C")

#solution(7, [ICSI — Intra Cytoplasmic Sperm Injection — picks one sperm with a fine needle and injects it straight into the egg's *cytoplasm*. It is the rescue technology when sperm cannot penetrate the egg on their own.], answer: "A")

#solution(8, [Gonorrhoea is caused by the bacterium *Neisseria gonorrhoeae*, so antibiotics cure it. Genital herpes (herpes simplex virus), hepatitis-B and AIDS (HIV) are all *viral* — treatable but never fully curable.], answer: "D")

#solution(9, [The first-trimester window runs *up to 12 weeks*, when termination is safest and one registered medical practitioner can certify it. The 12–24-week window needs practitioners' opinions, and beyond 24 weeks only narrow special cases qualify.], answer: "B")

#solution(10, [The *Pre-Conception and Pre-Natal Diagnostic Techniques Act, 1994* bans prenatal sex determination and sex-selective abortions, because misuse led to female foeticide. The diagnostic uses — chromosomal and metabolic testing — remain legal.], answer: "A")

